WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
Speaker 1: We have a voicemail number. That&nbsp;
number is two one nine two David Pakman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.840
This is a really important topic. I got&nbsp;
a caller who said, is there something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:18.640
about the news that is bad for one's health?
Speaker 7: Hi, David. My name is Anna, long time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:24.720
viewer of the show. I wanted to bring some female&nbsp;
representation to your voice, your questions. My&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:35.360
question for you is, how do you protect your&nbsp;
mental health while consuming so much horrible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.720
media? Yep. Like, I, I feel like my mental&nbsp;
health has suffered just from trying to follow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:48.800
the world's news and follow current events. And&nbsp;
I can't imagine what it's like for somebody that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.520
you know, does this as their&nbsp;
job. So I was wondering how&nbsp;

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:01.120
Speaker 1: how you deal with that. Yeah, many&nbsp;
people ask me this, so there's two things that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:08.480
go on. One is, I'll admit it, you become sort&nbsp;
of desensitized to it. I am deaf. I know when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:14.800
I'm talking to people not in this business, they&nbsp;
will report to me or they will mention some story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:20.720
in the news. And I can tell I'm not having the&nbsp;
visceral reaction they're having because I've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:24.800
been desensitized to a lot of the stuff. That's&nbsp;
number one. But number two, you've got to schedule&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:31.360
breaks. And when when I'm done producing Friday's&nbsp;
show, until I start getting ready for the Monday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.640
show, I'm not paying attention to any news unless&nbsp;
there's like some weekend political event going on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:42.720
that I'm involved in streaming or whatever the&nbsp;
case may be. And I'm just reading not politics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:48.240
reading history, science, whatever fiction&nbsp;
and doing other things. And I think it's of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:53.680
incredible importance to do that. So the mere&nbsp;
fact, Ana, that you're asking the question is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:58.800
